# Update README when functionality changes

Whenever you add, remove, or meaningfully change **user-facing** behavior in One Stop Planner, update [`README.md`](README.md) in the **same change**.

## What counts

- New screens, tabs, modals, menus, or navigation items
- New fields or behaviors for events, tasks, subtasks, meals, workouts, goals, groups
- Auth, sync, storage, or account UX changes
- New setup/deploy requirements (env vars, SQL, Vercel steps)

## What to edit in README.md

1. **Current functionality** — add or adjust the relevant table rows
2. **How the app works** / **Data model** — if save shape or sync behavior changed
3. **Tech stack** / **Project structure** — if new packages or major files were added
4. **Last major feature documented** (bottom of README) — one-line note of what just shipped

Do **not** remove setup/deploy sections unless they are wrong. Prefer editing tables over rewriting the whole file.

## Checklist before finishing a feature

- [ ] Feature implemented and consistent with existing UI patterns
- [ ] `README.md` reflects the new behavior
- [ ] Mention the README update briefly in the reply to the user
